meta {
  name: Swift Backtest Compare
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/experimental/swift/backtest/PLTR?date=2026-10-09&timeframe=M5
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  date: 2026-10-09
  timeframe: M5
  ~sessions: RTH
  ~count: 2000
}

headers {
  Accept: application/json
}

docs {
  # Experimental — Swift Trend Backtest (Production vs Experimental)

  Side-by-side backtest for ONE ticker on ONE day. Replays the SAME historical
  candle series through BOTH scanners and returns their signals together:

  - **production**   — the live `SwiftTrendScanner` (webull.supertrend 7/3,
                       webull.alerts.swift-scan thresholds).
  - **experimental** — the `ExperimentalSwiftTrendScanner` (experimental.swift
                       in application-experimental.yml): a FASTER Supertrend and
                       tuned thresholds, used to see whether a config change
                       catches a move earlier and how many extra (possibly false)
                       signals it adds.

  Reuses the production backtester + market-data layer verbatim — nothing in
  production code is changed. Detection/analysis only: no orders, no Telegram.

  ## Path
  - `/{ticker}` — any US stock symbol (need NOT be in the universe).

  ## Query
  - `date`      — ET date YYYY-MM-DD (default: today ET).
  - `timeframe` — bar size (default: experimental.swift.timeframe).
                  Native: M1, M5, M15, M30, M60, M120, M240.
                  SYNTHETIC: M2, M3 (and any M<n>) are built on the fly by
                  resampling M1 — the broker does not serve them natively.
  - `sessions`  — RTH, PRE, ATH, OVN (comma-separated; default: configured).
  - `count`     — bars to fetch back from NOW (auto-sized by default; older dates
                  need a larger count since the broker returns the most recent N).

  ## Response (200)
  {
    ticker, date, timeframe, sessions, barsFetched,
    production:   { config:{ supertrendLength, supertrendFactor, minTravelAtr,
                             minSeparationAtr, cooldownMinutes },
                    signalCount, swiftUpCount, swiftDownCount,
                    firstSignalEt, signals:[ "11:58 ET  🟢 UP  @ 205.36  ST ...  travel 2.20×ATR", ... ] },
    experimental: { ...same shape... },
    comparison:   { productionFirstSignalEt, experimentalFirstSignalEt,
                    experimentalEarlierByMinutes, extraSignalsFromExperimental, note }
  }

  Positive `experimentalEarlierByMinutes` = the experimental config fired sooner.
  Positive `extraSignalsFromExperimental` = it produced more signals (earlier
  entry traded for more potential false positives).

  ## Try these
  - PLTR 2026-10-09 M5  — production fired UP at 11:58 (late on the grind up).
  - PLTR 2026-10-09 M3  — synthetic 3-min; a faster Supertrend should flip sooner.
  - Change the ticker to backtest ANY stock on ANY day.

  ## Errors
  - `400` — invalid date/timeframe/session.
  - `502` — Webull market-data error (e.g. missing/invalid credentials).
  - `503` — no bars returned for the ticker.
}
